2026-09-23: join unconditional single-entry continuations during lowering.

RED: the array-minimum loop still had edge (6,5), an unconditional branch to
a unique-entry continuation requiring redundant block-argument copies. One
assertion failed, zero compilation errors. GREEN: bind those parameters
simultaneously to the preceding local definitions, append the unchanged
instructions in order, and retain the existing final terminator.
Source labels (including static relocation-only references), block_addr
targets, function entry, self edges and multiply-entered blocks are retained.
Indirect and asm-goto edges participate in entry counting. Local SSA and
memory/world remain explicit; no allocator/coalescing policy is changed.

Three structural controls cover operand permutation, effect-token identity,
indirect entries, label retention and malformed argument types/arity.
The C fixture covers volatile effects, both branches, loop iterations,
static label-table dispatch and dynamic local-object lifetimes. Both
interpreters pass with optimization off/on. Native EvoCC O2 and each of
GCC-14/Clang-19 O0/O2 exit zero in the offline sealed ARM64 environment.

Changed gate against 5eba25a: 1089 PASS, zero FAIL, three historical ignored;
Clippy all-targets -D warnings and fmt --check PASS. The first run passed all
tests but failed Clippy's while-let style check; it was corrected, not waived.
